From 581f3c3d77d23dabe4d6a118316240d9f1eb368b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Usty <usty@uase.tech>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 08:45:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] fix: per-car financial report - stat boxes stack
 one-per-row on mobile, text gets cut off at page edge

Real root cause found for the report's ugly, page-bloated layout:
the financial summary used display:grid with auto-fill and
minmax(140px,1fr) - looks like a proper multi-column grid on a wide
desktop browser, but on a mobile-width screen (this being a
primarily mobile app, and this modal's own maxWidth is 720px which
resolves down to the device's actual narrow viewport on a phone),
auto-fill correctly collapses to a single column once the container
is too narrow to fit a second 140px box plus its gap - explaining
exactly why this document needed 4 pages for content that should fit
in 1-2.

Switched to an explicit repeat(2,1fr) grid - always exactly 2
columns regardless of screen width, so the 6 stat boxes now take 3
rows instead of 6.

Also fixed the confirmed text-cutoff bug in the same file's Sale
Transaction table: a long unbroken string (an email address, no
spaces to wrap at) had no word-break/overflow-wrap property set, so
it overflowed straight past the page's right margin instead of
wrapping to a new line.
